    "description": "If your generator has a 50-amp outlet and you want to use all of it, you need a 50-amp inlet, and the PBN50 is the one we would choose. Retail and distributor listings describe it as a 50-amp, 125/250 volt inlet with a CS6375 connector, rated for generators up to 12,500 running watts, in an outdoor-rated, UV-stabilized ABS enclosure that meets NEMA 3R. The cord enters from the bottom under a flip-lid cover, and the box is cULus listed. Home Depot Canada lists a five-year warranty. The catch is space. Owner reviews say 6-gauge wire, which many electricians use on a 50-amp run, is tight in this box, and one reviewer says the terminals are designed around 8-gauge, so the electrician should check the terminal rating against the wire they plan to pull. Reliance also sells a steel, front-entry 50-amp box if you prefer metal. Neither makes sense on a generator whose biggest outlet is an L14-30."
